  "water_ground": {
    "_doc": "Ground height (m above the sea) of a settlement with water, by location number; others with water stand at 1.5 m. The water is at sea level whatever the ground: higher ground makes its water tiles deep ditches. North Britanny sits on land 7-11 m up: its stream is a ditch running into its pond.",
